{
  "id": "chapter-24",
  "number": 24,
  "title": "PAST. PRESENT. BECOMING.",
  "period": "Late September–October",
  "passages": [
    "Three crows gave the closing stretch a language: past, present, becoming. A garment still waiting to emerge. Costume season beginning. A kilt, a joke, another opportunity to play.",
    "The archive doesn't end with everything resolved. It ends with me still making things. Still entering rooms. Still curious about what comes next. Looking back, I can see the daily practices becoming a life: care for my body, room for expression, work made with my hands, and people willing to share the experience.",
    "Modern Day Circus is the record of that becoming. I am learning how to live a life I can recognize as my own—and how to let myself be seen while I live it."
  ],
  "reflections": [
    {
      "kind": "Notice",
      "prompt": "What are you still curious to become?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "Write",
      "prompt": "Write one thing you are carrying from the past, one thing you appreciate in the present, and one thing you are curious to become."
    },
    {
      "kind": "Try",
      "prompt": "Leave a note for yourself to open a month from now. Include one question you hope to keep exploring."
    }
  ],
